From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:57:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs(r48): name the phase-1b commit SHA and downgrade the f16
 gate claim

Section 11 now reads Commit: 6902a9bf6, which the phase-1b commit itself could
not carry. The f16_f32 row is corrected: test-backend-ops produces 0 cases for
type_a=q5_K,type_b=f16, so that registration is gated by inspection only and
neither its correctness nor the -30..-180% figure was exercised there.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-234 R48 Q5_K phase 1b, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - report-only, names the phase-1b commit SHA and adds the 63-* receipt
Lane: lane-234
---
 OPUS-R48-Q5K-MATVEC-REPORT.md     |  8 ++++----
 r48-evidence/63-test-q5k-f16b.rc  |  1 +
 r48-evidence/63-test-q5k-f16b.txt | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 r48-evidence/63-test-q5k-f16b.rc
 create mode 100644 r48-evidence/63-test-q5k-f16b.txt

diff --git a/OPUS-R48-Q5K-MATVEC-REPORT.md b/OPUS-R48-Q5K-MATVEC-REPORT.md
index 2736e9493..15558e533 100644
--- a/OPUS-R48-Q5K-MATVEC-REPORT.md
+++ b/OPUS-R48-Q5K-MATVEC-REPORT.md
@@ -475,7 +475,7 @@ no spec-constant arity change, so this is a host relink.
 |---|---|
 | `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp` `:7078` | New `q5k_b_hoist_for_cols(num_cols)` lambda next to the existing `q5k_b_hoist` env probe: returns `q5k_b_hoist` when `num_cols <= 3`, else `0`. `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0` still forces **every** width to `0` - the one-binary opt-out is unchanged. |
 | `ggml-vulkan.cpp` `:7115` | `f32_f32` Q5_K dmmv registration passes `q5k_b_hoist_for_cols(i+1)` as spec-constant element 3 instead of the bare `q5k_b_hoist`. |
-| `ggml-vulkan.cpp` `:7181` | `f16_f32` Q5_K dmmv registration, same substitution. **Not in the phase-1b brief, and load-bearing**: this registration sits in the same `for (i < mul_mat_vec_max_cols)` loop and was already passing the ungated `q5k_b_hoist`, so leaving it alone would have left the -30..-180% wide-width regression live on the f16-activation path. Same loop, same `i+1`, same one change. |
+| `ggml-vulkan.cpp` `:7181` | `f16_f32` Q5_K dmmv registration, same substitution. **Not in the phase-1b brief.** This registration sits in the same `for (i < mul_mat_vec_max_cols)` loop and was already passing the ungated `q5k_b_hoist`, so leaving it alone would have left the wide-width arm ungated on the f16-activation path. Same loop, same `i+1`, same one change - but **gated by inspection, not by measurement**: `test-backend-ops` produced **0 cases** for `type_a=q5_K,type_b=f16` (`r48-evidence/63-*`, 0/0 tests, rc 0), so neither the correctness nor the -30..-180% figure was exercised on this path. The regression is *assumed* to carry over from the f32 path by shared shader and shared spec constant. |
 | `ggml-vulkan.cpp` `:7257` | Q5_K `_id` registration left as-is. It passes a literal `NUM_COLS = 1`, so the gate is a no-op there by construction; changing it would alter nothing and add noise. |
 | `ggml-vulkan.cpp` `:7088` | Device-init receipt line now reads `q5_k mat-vec activation-hoist: ON (n<=3)` when enabled, `OFF` when forced off. The print sits outside the per-`i` loop and cannot know `i`, so the static `(n<=3)` string is the honest shape. |
 | `docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md` | New `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST` row. States the default is width-gated rather than a blanket ON, carries the pairing numbers, and marks the `<=3` boundary as a gfx1103 measurement, **not a portable constant**. |
@@ -491,6 +491,7 @@ explicit value - so the gate cannot be bypassed by a missed call site on this pa
 | Build | `ninja -C build-vulkan test-backend-ops` | `r48-evidence/60-build.txt` + `.rc` | 0 | - | - |
 | Gate ON (default) | `test -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0 -p "type_a=q5_K"` | `r48-evidence/61-test-q5k-gate-on.txt` + `.rc` | 0 | 61/61 | **0** |
 | Forced OFF | same, `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0` | `r48-evidence/62-test-q5k-hoist-off.txt` + `.rc` | 0 | 61/61 | **0** |
+| f16 activations | `test ... -p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f16"` | `r48-evidence/63-test-q5k-f16b.txt` + `.rc` | 0 | **0/0 - no such case exists** | 0 |
 
 Both test receipts capture stderr, so each one carries its own device-init line: `61-*` reads
 `activation-hoist: ON (n<=3)`, `62-*` reads `activation-hoist: OFF`. That is the proof the gate and
@@ -504,9 +505,8 @@ No perf was run in this phase, no `llama-*` binary was launched, no model was lo
 justified by HQ's pairing of the *ungated* default, not by a measurement of the gated one. What §11.1
 establishes is that the wide arm loses; what it does not establish is that the narrow arm wins.
 
-This section ships **in** the phase-1b commit, so it cannot name that commit's own SHA. The commit
-is the single one on this branch carrying `Lane: lane-234` and the subject
-`feat(vulkan): gate Q5_K mat-vec activation hoist to NUM_COLS<=3 (R48 phase 1b)`; `git log -1` names it.
+Commit: `6902a9bf6`. This paragraph and the f16 row above were corrected in the follow-up commit
+named by `git log -1`, because the phase-1b commit could not contain its own SHA.
 
 PHASE-R48-Q5K-1B-DONE
 
